{"author":{"id":"29588b87a98184856c6eb9104921c34cca98a9cb029a2ee86cc10622d693ba86"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794863634,"nonce":"1BYnu9OfhvKF1vwJvRY5K7DIc4c=","title":"text_area: double click does not select a word (triple click does not select the line)","message":"`text_input` and `code` select the word under the pointer on double click (via `text_edit::word_at_position`). `text_area` does not: a double click only places the cursor. The source says so (`text_area/handlers.rs`, comment around lines 147-157: \"text_area doesn't yet implement double-tap word selection\").\n\n\n- Double click selects the word under the pointer.\n- Triple click selects the line (paragraph).\n- Shift+click extends the selection from the anchor.\n- Same for the touch double-tap path, where the long-press timer is currently armed with `None` instead of a word callback.\n\n\nPointer down/up twice at the same spot only sets the cursor; `selection_start` stays `None`, nothing is highlighted.\n\nRepro output (text `\"hello world\\nsecond line\"`, click over \"world\"):\n\n```\nafter click 1: selection_start=None, cursor=(line 0, col 7)\nafter click 2: selection_start=None, cursor=(line 0, col 7)\nafter click 3: selection_start=None, cursor=(line 0, col 7)\n```\nExpected after click 2: selection (0,6)..(0,11).\n\n\n```rust\nuse blinc_core::events::event_types;\nuse blinc_layout::event_handler::EventContext;\nuse blinc_layout::renderer::RenderTree;\nuse blinc_layout::widgets::text_area::{text_area, text_area_state};\n\nfn double_click_selects_nothing() {\n    blinc_theme::ThemeState::init_default();\n    let state = text_area_state();\n    state.lock().unwrap().set_value(\"hello world\\nsecond line\");\n    let area = text_area(\u0026state).w(300.0).rows(4);\n    let mut tree = RenderTree::from_element(\u0026area);\n    tree.compute_layout(400.0, 300.0);\n    let root = tree.root().unwrap();\n    let h = blinc_layout::div::ElementBuilder::event_handlers(\u0026area).unwrap();\n    for _ in 0..2 {\n        for ty in [event_types::POINTER_DOWN, event_types::POINTER_UP] {\n            h.dispatch(\u0026EventContext::new(ty, root)\n                .with_bounds(300.0, 100.0).with_local_pos(70.0, 14.0));\n        }\n    }\n    // inspect state: selection_start (pub(crate)) is None; expected Some((0,6)) with cursor (0,11)\n}\n```\n\n\nBlinc fs-blinc-3.1 (cf925af); unchanged on current main. Linux, headless test, default theme.\n\n\nMirror the `text_input` pattern: count clicks on the data lock (time and position window), on the second click call `text_edit::word_at_position(line, column)` and set `selection_start`/`cursor`; on the third click select the whole logical line; pass the same closure to `arm_long_press_timer` for touch. For word boundaries, consider Unicode word segmentation (UAX #29, e.g. the `unicode-segmentation` crate) instead of an alphanumeric/space split, so non-Latin scripts and punctuation behave as in other toolkits.","files":null}]}